<comment datatype='string'>&lt;a href=&quot;/gene?orgid=META&amp;id=THLCLOS-MONOMER&quot;&gt;Acetoacetyl-CoA thiolase&lt;/a&gt; catalyzes the condensation of two &lt;a href=&quot;/compound?orgid=META&amp;id=ACETYL-COA&quot;&gt;acetyl-CoA&lt;/a&gt; molecules to form &lt;a href=&quot;/compound?orgid=META&amp;id=ACETOACETYL-COA&quot;&gt;acetoacetyl-CoA&lt;/a&gt;. The enzyme occupies an important position in the central fermentation pathway leading to production of either acids or solvents in &lt;a href=&quot;/META/NEW-IMAGE?object=TAX-1488&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Clostridium acetobutylicum&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/a&gt;. It lies at the branch point of these pathways and influences the flow of carbon into them.
&lt;p&gt;
The enzyme from &lt;a href=&quot;/META/NEW-IMAGE?object=TAX-272562&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Clostridium acetobutylicum&lt;/i&gt; ATCC 824&lt;/a&gt; has been purified 70-fold to homogeneity. Unlike the thiolase in &lt;a href=&quot;/META/NEW-IMAGE?object=TAX-1501&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Clostridium pasteurianum&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, the thiolase from &lt;a href=&quot;/META/NEW-IMAGE?object=TAX-1488&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Clostridium acetobutylicum&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/a&gt; has high relative activity throughout the physiological range of internal pH of 5.5 to 7.0, indicating that change in internal pH during acid production is not an important factor in the regulation of this thiolase. The thiolase is inhibited by micromolar levels of CoA, and by ATP and &lt;a href=&quot;/compound?orgid=META&amp;id=BUTYRYL-COA&quot;&gt;butanoyl-CoA&lt;/a&gt; [&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/16347774&quot;&gt;Wiesenborn88&lt;/a&gt;].
&lt;p&gt;
The &lt;a href=&quot;/gene?orgid=META&amp;id=G-96&quot;&gt;thl&lt;/a&gt; gene encoding the enzyme has been cloned by using primary antibodies raised to the purified enzyme [&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/1685080&quot;&gt;Petersen91a&lt;/a&gt;] and subsequently sequenced [&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/7867955&quot;&gt;StimHerndon95&lt;/a&gt;].
&lt;p&gt;
Thiolase may also play an indirect role in acid uptake during solventogenesis</comment>
